{"ts": "2026-10-16T09:25:13.726260Z", "run_id": "r-20261016T0920Z-ec4a", "unit": "openspec:add-telemetry-runtime", "seq": 35, "type": "task.done", "task": "1.2", "base": "77d99294102f10e9f775599e64b3bf37a72e1d3e", "parents": [], "notes": "Accepted findings handled, by id. F-4dc92 (relevant here): the spec says otlp_receiver.spans() 'contains x' without saying name or tuple. The red test reads it as the span NAME over (name, attrs) tuples; spans() returns (name, resource-attributes dict) tuples as the requirement demands, so both readings are satisfied. F-4dc92's other clauses (subprocess inherits MINTMORY_OTEL_ENABLED=false, how to patch _endpoint_reachable in the child, and the leaked shutdown-daemon thread event) concern scenarios of tasks 3.1 and 5.1, not task 1.2's fixtures, so they are untouched here. F-1619b9, F-0ad188, F-fea82d and F-5d64eb concern exporter parsing/scrubbing/global-provider scenarios of tasks 3-8 and are also untouched. No business/product decisions were made; no new # noqa or # type: ignore added.", "suppressions": []}
